  ],
  "slug": "neuronal-state-4725",
  "summary": "Recent preprints pair organoid and single-cell datasets with benchmarking, segmentation and curation tools aimed at reproducible, standardized analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The four preprints share a computational emphasis on resolving cellular heterogeneity and maturation state in organoid and tissue-derived systems. A transcriptomic framework integrates single-cell and single-nucleus data from 11 kidney organoid, assembloid and transplantation studies to benchmark maturation across models. Organotchi provides an open-source pipeline for brightfield segmentation, ten-feature morphological profiling and longitudinal tracking of neural organoids. TRACE establishes a traceable curation workflow, demonstrated by a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource. SSAF-T adds a segmentation-free agentic approach to cell-type inference in spatial transcriptomics. What is new is the emphasis on standardized benchmarking and reproducible resource construction rather than purely descriptive profiling; the items do not demonstrate cross-system transfer of these methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
